invariant: INV-16
file: gcm.c
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: multiply_by_subkey adds the running multiple into the product
  when the accumulator bit is set, through a 0xff mask. Written as an if
  on that bit, the bit decides which path runs -- and under a
  -DCH_SUITE_AES_GCM build the accumulator is derived from the hash
  subkey, so the branch is on the key. This is the select poly1305_final
  and cswap already carry, in the one file no codegen gate compiled until
  gcm.c joined BRANCH_SRCS. The branch count is what reads it: the
  multiply tokens see nothing here, and every clang spec emits more
  conditional branches in gcm.c than its ceiling records
  (https://github.com/c4milo/chapulin/issues/141).

--- old
        uint8_t selected = (uint8_t)(0U - selected_bit); // 0xff when the bit is set, else 0
        for (size_t i = 0; i < AES_BLOCK; i++) {
            product[i] = (uint8_t)(product[i] ^ (multiple[i] & selected));
        }
--- new
        if (selected_bit != 0) {
            for (size_t i = 0; i < AES_BLOCK; i++) {
                product[i] = (uint8_t)(product[i] ^ multiple[i]);
            }
        }
